---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = 'September 7, 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Service — Greg Weinger"
  description="The terms that govern your use of gweinger.com and its content."
>
  <div class="container legal">

    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="lead">The short version: this site is here to help. Use it, share it, but don't mistake it for professional advice or copy it wholesale.</p>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      By using gweinger.com, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree with them, please
      don't use the site. The site is operated by Greg Weinger as a personal publication
      supporting <em>The Introverted Leader</em> podcast.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is — and isn't</h2>
    <p>
      Everything here is educational and informational. The podcast, articles, newsletters,
      and masterclass share ideas and frameworks about leadership
      and career growth for introverted professionals.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>It is not professional advice.</strong> Nothing on this site constitutes career
      counseling, legal advice, medical or mental health advice, financial advice, or an
      employment relationship. Guests share their own experience and opinions, which are
      theirs and not necessarily mine. Decisions about your career, your health, and your
      workplace are yours to make — consult a qualified professional when the stakes call
      for one.
    </p>
    <p>
      I make no promise that any technique described here will produce a particular result,
      including a promotion, a raise, or any specific career outcome.
    </p>

    <h2>Content and intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The written content, podcast episodes, and original graphics on this site belong to
      Greg Weinger unless credited otherwise. You're welcome to quote short excerpts with
      attribution and a link back. You may not republish full episodes, transcripts, or
      articles, or use this content to train commercial machine learning models, without
      written permission.
    </p>
    <p>
      Guest names, book titles, company names, and logos belong to their respective owners
      and appear here for identification and commentary.
    </p>

    <h2>Free programs and events</h2>
    <p>
      The masterclass is offered free of charge. I may change its format or availability,
      or discontinue it, at any time. Signing up doesn't create any contractual obligation on
      either side beyond my intention to provide it as described.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links and disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      Some outbound links — typically to books discussed on the show — are affiliate links.
      If you buy through one, I may earn a small commission at no additional cost to you.
      This never changes what I recommend or what a guest says. Recommendations reflect
      genuine opinion, not commercial arrangement.
    </p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      This site links out to guest websites, podcast platforms, and other resources. I don't
      control those sites and I'm not responsible for their content, accuracy, or practices.
      Following an external link is at your own discretion.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the contact form to send spam, solicitations, or abusive messages</li>
      <li>Attempt to disrupt, overload, or gain unauthorized access to the site</li>
      <li>Scrape the site in a way that degrades it for other visitors</li>
      <li>Misrepresent yourself or impersonate someone else when contacting me</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Availability</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided "as is." I try to keep it accurate and online, but I don't
      guarantee that it will be uninterrupted, error-free, or that any particular content
      will remain available.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, Greg Weinger is not liable for any indirect,
      incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of this site or reliance on
      its content. Some jurisdictions don't allow these limitations, in which case they
      apply only as far as the law permits.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      I may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top of this page reflects
      the current version, and continued use of the site after an update means you accept
